1
00:00:03,207 --> 00:00:08,426
Open Reports, Artificial Intelligence Reports, and AI Chat Session Analytics.

2
00:00:08,426 --> 00:00:12,640
Choose a Date range, such as the last 30 days, and a profile,

3
00:00:12,640 --> 00:00:14,967
or any profile, and click Show.

4
00:00:15,418 --> 00:00:20,477
Conversation and Usage shows the Total Sessions and the Unique Visitors, the Containment

5
00:00:20,477 --> 00:00:24,999
Rate, the share of chats that the assistant handled alone, and the Abandonment

6
00:00:24,999 --> 00:00:28,498
Rate, the share where the person left without a resolution.

7
00:00:28,948 --> 00:00:33,528
It also shows how long chats last and how many messages they have,

8
00:00:33,528 --> 00:00:35,818
and how many people come back.

9
00:00:35,818 --> 00:00:40,588
Resolved, Abandoned and Active Sessions count the chats by their end.

10
00:00:41,039 --> 00:00:44,104
The usage by time of day and by day of the week show

11
00:00:44,104 --> 00:00:48,119
when people chat, so that you can have staff ready for the busy hours.

12
00:00:48,570 --> 00:00:53,071
User Segmentation separates signed-in users from anonymous visitors.

13
00:00:53,071 --> 00:00:57,875
Model and System Performance shows the response time and the tokens used:

14
00:00:57,875 --> 00:01:02,680
the input tokens that are sent, and the output tokens that the AI writes.

15
00:01:03,131 --> 00:01:08,467
Resolution and Conversion shows how many finished chats the AI judged resolved, and

16
00:01:08,467 --> 00:01:11,045
the average score against your goals.

17
00:01:11,045 --> 00:01:13,264
User Feedback shows the thumbs:

18
00:01:13,264 --> 00:01:17,221
the satisfaction rate, and how many chats were rated at all.

19
00:01:17,672 --> 00:01:21,752
Export as CSV downloads the chats behind the report.

